Seam: chrome/browser/ui/webui/settings/BUILD.gn, source_set("impl") -- the
      target settings_clear_browsing_data_handler.cc and
      settings_localized_strings_provider.cc build in.
Why: GN wiring for patches 0192, 0262 and 0270. Those hooks include
     //arcium/ui/browser and //arcium/common headers, and this target has no
     dep, direct or transitive, on any Arcium target or on //chrome/browser/ui,
     so `gn check` rejects the includes outright.

     Every Arcium dep this target needs is added here rather than beside the
     hook that needs it, so that no two patches touch this file: a patch whose
     added lines sit inside another's context cannot be told apart from a
     conflict once both are applied, and scripts/sync then reports one on
     every run.

     No cycle: //arcium/ui/browser and //arcium/common depend on nothing that
     reaches back into this target, so `gn gen` accepts the graph.
Delegates to: nothing. GN wiring carries no call.

